            {"question":"According to the lecture, the majority of centenarians will be:","options":["Men","Women","Equally divided between men and women","Children of elderly parents"],"answer":"Women"},
            {"question":"Which statement about normal age-related physical changes is MOST correct?","options":["They occur suddenly and are identical in all people.","They are gradual and vary in rate and degree among individuals.","They occur only when disease is present.","They are completely preventable through medication."],"answer":"They are gradual and vary in rate and degree among individuals."},
            {"question":"Which factor may increase the speed and degree of age-related physical changes?","options":["Disease","Age classification only","Education","Occupation only"],"answer":"Disease"},
            {"question":"Which combination can influence the rate and degree of age-related changes?","options":["Lifestyle, nutrition, economic status, and social environment","Blood group, height, and eye color","Occupation only","Education and marital status only"],"answer":"Lifestyle, nutrition, economic status, and social environment"},
            {"question":"Recognizing normal age-related changes can help an older adult:","options":["Stop the aging process","Adapt and cope with the changes","Avoid all medical care","Prevent all physical changes"],"answer":"Adapt and cope with the changes"},
