            {"question":"Which combination contains only symptoms listed under other symptoms of Parkinson's disease?","options":["Constipation, urinary incontinence, depression, dementia","Rigidity, bradykinesia, tremor, depression","Postural instability, rigidity, constipation, tremor","Tremor, micrographia, dementia, rigidity"],"answer":"Constipation, urinary incontinence, depression, dementia"},
            {"question":"Which statement regarding the diagnosis of Parkinson's disease is MOST correct?","options":["There is one definitive diagnostic laboratory test.","Diagnosis is based only on PET scanning.","Medical history and neurological tests are used because no definitive test exists.","Diagnosis is made only after dementia develops."],"answer":"Medical history and neurological tests are used because no definitive test exists."},
            {"question":"PET scans may assist in Parkinson's disease by determining:","options":["Acetylcholine levels","Dopamine levels","Calcium levels","Blood glucose levels"],"answer":"Dopamine levels"},
