            {"question":"The nurse should assess behavioral problems including:","options":["Pain, constipation, hunger, and disruptive behavior","Fever, rash, and cough only","Hearing and vision only","Blood pressure and pulse only"],"answer":"Pain, constipation, hunger, and disruptive behavior"},
            {"question":"When assessing a patient with tremor, the nurse should specifically distinguish between:","options":["Parkinson's tremor and essential tremor","Parkinson's tremor and fever","Essential tremor and constipation","Rigidity and depression"],"answer":"Parkinson's tremor and essential tremor"},
            {"question":"A 70-year-old patient has a tremor that is most prominent while the muscles are relaxed and decreases during voluntary movement. Which type of tremor is MOST likely?","options":["Essential tremor","Parkinson's disease tremor","Action-only tremor","Postural tremor"],"answer":"Parkinson's disease tremor"},
            {"question":"A patient develops tremor while holding a cup and while keeping the arms outstretched. The tremor disappears at rest. Which finding BEST supports the diagnosis of essential/senile tremor?","options":["Resting tremor","Action/postural tremor","Pill-rolling tremor","Unilateral onset"],"answer":"Action/postural tremor"},
