            {"question":"A patient receiving Levodopa/carbidopa develops nausea, vomiting, hypotension, and mental changes. The nurse should recognize these findings as:","options":["Listed adverse effects of the medication","Signs of essential tremor","Cardinal manifestations of PD","Expected effects of Artane"],"answer":"Listed adverse effects of the medication"},
            {"question":"A patient receiving Artane complains of dry mouth and blurred vision and appears confused. Which explanation is MOST consistent with the lecture?","options":["These are listed adverse effects of anticholinergic therapy.","These findings indicate dopamine excess.","These findings represent postural instability.","These findings confirm essential tremor."],"answer":"These are listed adverse effects of anticholinergic therapy."},
