            {"question":"Which symptom is described as a common marker of osteoarthritis and is often most noticeable:","options":["At the end of vigorous exercise only","First thing in the morning or after prolonged inactivity","Only during sleep","Immediately after eating"],"answer":"First thing in the morning or after prolonged inactivity"},
            {"question":"An elderly patient reports joint stiffness after sitting in a car for a prolonged period. According to the lecture, this stiffness usually:","options":["Persists for several hours","Resolves within 30 minutes of light activity","Requires complete bed rest","Progressively worsens with light activity"],"answer":"Resolves within 30 minutes of light activity"},
            {"question":"Which finding represents loss of range of motion in osteoarthritis?","options":["Joint becomes more flexible after prolonged inactivity","Joint may become less flexible despite warming up","Joint always regains full motion after activity","Joint movement becomes completely painless"],"answer":"Joint may become less flexible despite warming up"},
            {"question":"An OA patient develops swelling because of excess fluid buildup around the joint. Which additional findings are mentioned with swelling?","options":["Fever, redness, and warmth","Pallor, cyanosis, and coldness","Numbness, paralysis, and tremor","Bruising, bleeding, and ulceration"],"answer":"Fever, redness, and warmth"},
            {"question":"Which joint change may result in a noticeable physical deformity?","options":["Bone spurs and other joint changes","Increased muscle flexibility","Decreased body weight","Improved joint lubrication"],"answer":"Bone spurs and other joint changes"},
            {"question":"An OA patient has enlarged finger joints and knees that appear bowlegged. These findings are most consistent with:","options":["Loss of appetite","Joint deformity","Joint instability only","Normal aging without joint changes"],"answer":"Joint deformity"},
            {"question":"Which of the following is listed as a sign of osteoarthritis?","options":["Crepitus during movement","Increased range of motion","Complete absence of tenderness","Severe systemic infection"],"answer":"Crepitus during movement"},
            {"question":"Which combination contains findings that are all listed as signs of osteoarthritis?","options":["Crepitus, limited ROM, joint tenderness","Increased ROM, muscle hypertrophy, bradycardia","Cyanosis, paralysis, hyperreflexia","Fever, severe hypotension, tachycardia"],"answer":"Crepitus, limited ROM, joint tenderness"},
            {"question":"Which finding indicates instability of an osteoarthritic joint?","options":["Joint instability","Improved flexibility","Increased range of motion","Absence of pain"],"answer":"Joint instability"},
            {"question":"Bone spurs in osteoarthritis are associated with:","options":["Friction and pressure between joint bones","Increased muscle activity","Improved cartilage formation","Decreased joint pressure"],"answer":"Friction and pressure between joint bones"},
            {"question":"A patient with osteoarthritis has increasing difficulty using the affected joint normally. This represents:","options":["Loss of functioning","Improved mobility","Increased joint flexibility","Normal joint adaptation"],"answer":"Loss of functioning"},
            {"question":"Which of the following is part of the physical examination for osteoarthritis?","options":["Joint tenderness","Blood glucose only","Lung expansion","Visual acuity"],"answer":"Joint tenderness"},
            {"question":"Which finding would NOT be expected as one of the physical examination findings listed for OA?","options":["Crepitus","Limited range of motion","Joint instability","Increased joint range of motion"],"answer":"Increased joint range of motion"},
            {"question":"Which statement about laboratory testing in osteoarthritis is MOST correct?","options":["There is a standard laboratory test that confirms OA.","Laboratory tests may help rule out other problems such as rheumatoid arthritis.","Blood testing is the primary method used to confirm OA.","Laboratory testing is never performed."],"answer":"Laboratory tests may help rule out other problems such as rheumatoid arthritis."},
            {"question":"Which procedure may involve drawing fluid from the joint during investigation of osteoarthritis?","options":["Arthrocentesis","Dexa scan","MRI","X-ray"],"answer":"Arthrocentesis"},
            {"question":"Which imaging method is typically used to confirm the diagnosis of osteoarthritis?","options":["MRI","X-ray","Dexa scan","Blood test"],"answer":"X-ray"},
            {"question":"An X-ray is performed on a patient suspected of having OA. Which finding can the X-ray reveal according to the lecture?","options":["Asymmetric joint-space narrowing","Increased cartilage thickness","Complete restoration of joint space","Increased muscle density"],"answer":"Asymmetric joint-space narrowing"},
            {"question":"Why is MRI used less often than X-rays in osteoarthritis?","options":["MRI cannot show cartilage","MRI is less sensitive than X-ray","Cost and availability","MRI cannot show bone"],"answer":"Cost and availability"},
            {"question":"According to the lecture, MRI scans can show:","options":["Cartilage, bone, and ligaments","Only blood vessels","Only muscle","Only joint fluid"],"answer":"Cartilage, bone, and ligaments"},
            {"question":"The primary purpose of the Dexa scan mentioned in the lecture is to measure:","options":["Joint temperature","Percentage of mineral density","Joint fluid volume","Muscle strength"],"answer":"Percentage of mineral density"},
            {"question":"Which statement regarding treatment of osteoarthritis is MOST correct?","options":["There is a definitive cure for OA with medication.","There is no cure, but medications and non-drug therapies can relieve pain.","Surgery is always the first treatment.","Nonpharmacological treatment has no role."],"answer":"There is no cure, but medications and non-drug therapies can relieve pain."},
            {"question":"Which medications are classified as analgesics in the lecture?","options":["Acetaminophen and opioids","Aspirin and ibuprofen only","Duloxetine and pregabalin","Corticosteroids only"],"answer":"Acetaminophen and opioids"},
            {"question":"Which group represents NSAIDs listed in the lecture?","options":["Aspirin, ibuprofen, diclofenac, celecoxib","Acetaminophen, opioids, duloxetine","Pregabalin, corticosteroids, opioids","Acetaminophen, aspirin, pregabalin"],"answer":"Aspirin, ibuprofen, diclofenac, celecoxib"},
            {"question":"According to the lecture, NSAIDs are commonly used to:","options":["Ease inflammation and pain","Increase joint deformity","Restore cartilage completely","Increase bone density"],"answer":"Ease inflammation and pain"},
